** PICKED TASKS

**Rtree
 * only supports primitive numeral data_type_infos as key, and has uint32_t dimensions
 * hyper rectangle is an n dimensional rectangle
 * void* get_hyper_rectangle(const void* hyper_context, void* record_tuple, tuple_def* record_def, pam_p, pmm_p, const void* transaction_id, int* abort_error); should return dimensions, number of pairs each being pair of same type numeral type_info number
 * STATIC_POSITION(0) - low value, STATIC_POSITION(1) - high value of the 0th dimension, they may point to the same positional_accessor
 * find a way to get area without multiplication, or some other way, that is a robust policy to split and merge without this area value
   * contender : splits and merges happen according to the minimal increase in interior node bounding boxes
 * very similar to b+tree, n dimensional data can be searched, inserted, deleted, no least_keys_page_id required
 * inserts walk down only 1 path of the tree, trying to minimize the increased area, or use some other policy
 * searches walk down a tree, and maintain a stack, releasing locks only if only 1 entry is to be scaned in the interior node, in READ_LOCK
   * next, prev and get_curr are always supported, in WRITE_LOCK and READ_LOCK_INTERIOR_WRITE_LOCK_LEAF deletes/inserts and modifies_non_key_element (if we are in right rectangle), updates are supported
 * you need to define a rtree_tuple_definitions, it must have a list of data_type_info, all primitive numeral types
 * need utilities
   * to find collective hyper_rectangle tuple from given two hyper_rectangle tuples -> minimum of the min values, and maximum of the max values
   * to find intersecting hyper_rectangle tuple from the given two hyper_rectangle tuples -> maximum of the min values, and minimum of the max values
   * to check if one contains another, all dimensions of 1 conatins the dimensions of the another
   * to make sure the hyper_rectangle tuple is valid, minX <= maxX
   * to find the area of the given hyper_rectangle tuple -> with right ideas we may not need these
 * iterators to find the intersecting hyper_rectangle tuples OR containing hyper_rectangle tuples
 * all interior nodes store a hyper rectangle and a corresponding page_id, and atleast 2 entries must fit on a page, else rttd contruction fails. yet you can have any number of dimensions.
 * there can be any number of dimensions, as long as 2 the user's tuples fit on leaf page and 2 interior entry tuples (with min,max ... list of dimensions -> child_page_id) fit on an interior page
 * keys will have a even count and all of numeral types, for ith dimension lower bound would be 2*i th key element and 2*i+1 will be upper bound, up to d dimentions (0 <= i < 2*d).
